-- A TYPICALLY on a rule's input or a record's field may be an expression, but not
-- one that reads a section input (TYPICALLY-ONE-BEHAVIOUR-SPEC.md W7, §4.3,
-- decision 1). A section input's own default is worked out once, from the values
-- the whole case gives. A default on a rule's input or a record's field is copied
-- to every call or construction that leaves it out, so what it reads there would
-- depend on the call, and R8 does not say where it is to be worked out.

GIVETH A NUMBER
phi MEANS 8

§ `Rates`
    GIVEN alpha IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 2
          -- fine: a section input's own default may read another section input
          beta IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY (alpha PLUS 1)

-- ERROR: reads `alpha` directly
GIVEN base IS A NUMBER
      rate IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY (phi PLUS alpha)
GIVETH A NUMBER
scaled MEANS base TIMES rate

-- ERROR: reads `alpha` through a definition
GIVETH A NUMBER
`alpha doubled` MEANS alpha TIMES 2

GIVEN base IS A NUMBER
      rate IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY `alpha doubled`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`scaled twice` MEANS base TIMES rate

-- ERROR: a record's field
DECLARE Budget HAS
  limit IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY (phi TIMES alpha)
  spent IS A NUMBER

-- No error: a definition that reads no section input has one value wherever it
-- is taken
GIVEN base IS A NUMBER
      rate IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY (phi PLUS 1)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`scaled by phi` MEANS base TIMES rate

-- No error: this default supplies the section input it would otherwise read, so
-- it reads none
GIVEN base IS A NUMBER
      rate IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY (`alpha doubled` WITH alpha IS 1)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`scaled supplied` MEANS base TIMES rate
